{"parentUuid":"10f2cc40-0247-4abb-8424-5b8c713e5e8e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"13e7b0d5-8762-466a-af93-ddfddd86e601","agentId":"a58a4d8ac806ce0e8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01956poUF8up6dT6VgspYQia","type":"tool_result","content":"# CUORE — E2E re-test #5: Scan wizard, Freeze-frame panel, Health, Scans list/diff, Job step 7 Mode 06, Messages/History\n\n**Tested:** `ZASFAKPN5J7B88115` (the Stelvio), against a throwaway `CUORE_STATE_DIR` per\ncheckpoint, each seeded *only* with the real `2026-10-13` lines copied verbatim out of\n`C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl` (read-only source, never written to), on this review's\nown uvicorn server with `cuore.live.ops` monkeypatched with the fakes from\n`cuore/tests/check_fullscan.py` (so the wizard/freeze panel work with no real adapter). Never the\nlive `:5000` instance, never COM3. Headless Edge, one instance at a time (a fresh profile per\ncheckpoint), cleaned up via `cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py`'s own `kill_edge_profile`. Driven over\nraw CDP (websockets), same posture as `cuore/tests/check_bench.py` -- real clicks on the actual\non-screen controls wherever the task called for a walk-through, not raw HTTP calls standing in for\nthem. Run as six independent, synchronous per-checkpoint scripts (`cp1_wizard.py` .. `cp6_messages.py`,\nsharing `common.py`/`server_app.py`, all in this session's scratchpad -- not committed to the repo),\neach with its own fresh server+browser+state dir, so a cut-off leaves this file current through the\nlast completed checkpoint and no single long-running process to kill mid-flight.\n=====\n# CUORE 0.1.0 — Typography, HTML & CSS audit + fix spec\n\n**For:** Claude Code (implementation)\n**Audited:** 2026-10-14, live app at `http://127.0.0.1:5000`, vehicle `ZASFAKPN5J7B88115`\n**Method:** computed-style extraction (fonts, sizes, weights, contrast, overflow, tap targets, stacking) + screenshots, dark and light theme, at a **485 px viewport** (Chrome side-panel width — effectively the phone layout). Desktop ≥1024 px was **not** tested; re-run the verification script in §7 there after fixing.\n**Layers covered:** global shell (header, vehicle strip, tab nav, footer, FAB), Bench, Job steps 1–12 + stepper + sticky bars, Record-result dialog, Hypotheses, Codes table, Code detail, Tests, Systems graph, Full scan, Liveboard, Report.\n\nStylesheets in play: `cuore.css` (492 rules), `flow.css`, `icons.css`, `print.css`, `fullscan.css`, `liveboard.css`, `feedback.css`, plus 3 inline rules. 675 rules total, **51 `!important`**.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Root causes (fix these first — they clear ~60 % of the symptoms)\n\n| # | Root cause | Symptoms it produces |\n|---|---|---|","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a3c6e46f-c521-4bff-b637-6006ed67c9e9","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:45:35.107Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# CUORE — E2E re-test #5: Scan wizard, Freeze-frame panel, Health, Scans list/diff, Job step 7 Mode 06, Messages/History\n\n**Tested:** `ZASFAKPN5J7B88115` (the Stelvio), against a throwaway `CUORE_STATE_DIR` per\ncheckpoint, each seeded *only* with the real `2026-10-13` lines copied verbatim out of\n`C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl` (read-only source, never written to), on this review's\nown uvicorn server with `cuore.live.ops` monkeypatched with the fakes from\n`cuore/tests/check_fullscan.py` (so the wizard/freeze panel work with no real adapter). Never the\nlive `:5000` instance, never COM3. Headless Edge, one instance at a time (a fresh profile per\ncheckpoint), cleaned up via `cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py`'s own `kill_edge_profile`. Driven over\nraw CDP (websockets), same posture as `cuore/tests/check_bench.py` -- real clicks on the actual\non-screen controls wherever the task called for a walk-through, not raw HTTP calls standing in for\nthem. Run as six independent, synchronous per-checkpoint scripts (`cp1_wizard.py` .. `cp6_messages.py`,\nsharing `common.py`/`server_app.py`, all in this session's scratchpad -- not committed to the repo),\neach with its own fresh server+browser+state dir, so a cut-off leaves this file current through the\nlast completed checkpoint and no single long-running process to kill mid-flight.\n=====\n# CUORE 0.1.0 — Typography, HTML & CSS audit + fix spec\n\n**For:** Claude Code (implementation)\n**Audited:** 2026-10-14, live app at `http://127.0.0.1:5000`, vehicle `ZASFAKPN5J7B88115`\n**Method:** computed-style extraction (fonts, sizes, weights, contrast, overflow, tap targets, stacking) + screenshots, dark and light theme, at a **485 px viewport** (Chrome side-panel width — effectively the phone layout). Desktop ≥1024 px was **not** tested; re-run the verification script in §7 there after fixing.\n**Layers covered:** global shell (header, vehicle strip, tab nav, footer, FAB), Bench, Job steps 1–12 + stepper + sticky bars, Record-result dialog, Hypotheses, Codes table, Code detail, Tests, Systems graph, Full scan, Liveboard, Report.\n\nStylesheets in play: `cuore.css` (492 rules), `flow.css`, `icons.css`, `print.css`, `fullscan.css`, `liveboard.css`, `feedback.css`, plus 3 inline rules. 675 rules total, **51 `!important`**.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Root causes (fix these first — they clear ~60 % of the symptoms)\n\n| # | Root cause | Symptoms it produces |\n|---|---|---|","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"55da71be-8364-4b75-b939-2443a68c5bd9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":20,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"github","host":"github.com","remote":"dangelojohn/CUORE","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"10f